## Deploying

### Prerequisites

- [Databricks CLI](https://docs.databricks.com/en/dev-tools/cli/databricks-cli.html) ≥ v0.288.0
- Dev, staging, and prod workspaces with Unity Catalog enabled
- Catalogs: `dev`, `{{ .input_staging_catalog_name }}`, `{{ .input_prod_catalog_name }}`, `{{ .input_test_catalog_name }}`

### 1. Configure your dev workspace

Open `databricks.yml` and fill in the `TODO` under `targets.dev.workspace.host` with your dev workspace URL.

### 2. Deploy to dev

```bash
# Validate the bundle
databricks bundle validate

# Deploy resources (job definitions, model registry, experiment, app)
databricks bundle deploy
```

The default target is `dev`. To deploy to other targets:

```bash
databricks bundle deploy -t staging
databricks bundle deploy -t prod
```

## Running the pipeline

After deploying, run the two jobs in order from the Databricks workspace UI or via CLI.

### Step 1: Data preparation

Runs `DataIngestion.py` → `DataPreprocessing.py` → `VectorSearch.py` as a scheduled job.

```bash
databricks bundle run data_preprocessing_job
```

This ingests documentation from a URL, chunks it into a preprocessed Delta table, and builds a Vector Search index.

### Step 2: Agent development

Runs `Agent.py` → `AgentEvaluation.py` → `ModelServing.py` as a scheduled job.

```bash
databricks bundle run agent_development_job
```

This creates Unity Catalog functions, logs the LangGraph agent with MLflow, evaluates it with LLM judges, and deploys it to a Mosaic AI serving endpoint.

### Step 3: Launch the chat interface

After `ModelServing.py` completes, it creates an agent serving endpoint. Set the `agent_serving_endpoint` variable in `databricks.yml` (if not auto-generated), then redeploy:

```bash
databricks bundle deploy
```

The Databricks App (`{{template `project_name_with_dashes` .}}-chatbot`) will be live and connected to your agent endpoint.

## Customizing this project

| What to customize | Where |
|-------------------|-------|
| Data source URL | `data_preparation/DataIngestion.py` — change `data_source_url` widget default |
| Chunking strategy | `data_preparation/DataPreprocessing.py` — adjust tokenizer/splitter settings |
| Agent tools | `agent_development/Agent.py` — add/remove UC function definitions and tool list in `app.py` |
| LLM model | `agent_development/app.py` — change `ChatDatabricks(endpoint=...)` |
| Eval dataset | `agent_development/AgentEvaluation.py` — replace the Parquet URL with your own eval set |
| Chat UI | `agent_deployment/chat_interface_deployment/app.py` |
| Job schedules | `resources/data-preparation-resource.yml` and `resources/agent-resource.yml` |
| Catalog/schema names | `databricks.yml` variables section |

